{"alignments": [{"id": "JOB.18.16.a001", "note": "מִתַּחַת → beneath fused (rule 30). Two prepositions with neither carrying content the other lacks: rule 23 heads such a compound on the governing morpheme standing first, as מֵעַל → from and מֵאֵת → of head on מִן; the English word 'beneath' does not choose the source head. Competing reading heads on תַּחַת as the sense-bearing morpheme.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.18.16.001", "WLC.JOB.18.16.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.18.16.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JOB.18.16.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.18.16.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.18.16.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JOB.18.16.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.18.16.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.18.16.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JOB.18.16.a004", "note": "'dried up' phrasal, headed on the verb (rule 44).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.18.16.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.18.16.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004", "t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JOB.18.16.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.18.16.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.18.16.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JOB.18.16.a006", "note": "מִמַּעַל → above fused (rule 30). The adverb מַעַל is a lexical content morpheme the preposition lacks (as מַעְלָה → above heads on it under rule 32), so rule 23's first sentence heads here; competing reading treats it as a pair of particles and heads on מִן.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.18.16.007", "WLC.JOB.18.16.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.18.16.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JOB.18.16.a007", "note": "'cut off' phrasal, discontinuous around the subject (rule 25); margin 'wither' set aside (rule 38).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.18.16.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.18.16.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010",